      "source": [
        "## 2. The question: decision, action, cost of a wrong call\n",
        "\n",
        "**What decision does this improve?**\n",
        "It improves the decision of *which pages should be reviewed and refreshed first* out of an inventory of thousands of content pages.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Who acts on the output, and what do they do?**\n",
        "Content editors and SEO strategists. They will consume the top of the ranked queue, inspect the specific diagnostic signals (reason codes), and update the page content (metadata, text, structure) or mark it for consolidation/monitoring.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What does a wrong recommendation cost?**\n",
        "- **False Positive (ranking a healthy page high for refresh):** Wastes human editorial hours auditing a page that did not need modification.\n",
        "- **False Negative (missing a page that is declining):** Results in lost organic impressions, clicks, conversions, and client search share.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why does data/ML help?**\n",
        "A simple fixed rule (e.g., \"refresh every page older than 180 days\") is too simple; it ignores search interest and position signals. Organic decay is caused by a tangled mix of signals (CTR, impression volume, rank position, update recency) that vary by client. A trained ML model can capture these non-linear relationships to rank refresh priorities far better than simple heuristics.\n",
        "\n",
        "**One-Paragraph Frame:**\n",
        "For content editors, deciding which pages to review and refresh first, we will build a ranked opportunity score from search console and analytics data, predicting the likelihood of content decline measured by Precision@50 and Average Precision. A wrong call costs wasted editor hours or lost search traffic. A plain rule isn't enough because multiple signals (CTR, impressions, age, position) are tangled and shift over time. We will claim only observed, directional, and decision-support results."
      ],
      "id": "2P-c1ipazK4c"
    },
