        "## 4. Careful words: what I can and can't claim\n",
        "\n",
        "**What my work will be able to claim:**\n",
        "- **Observed Associations:** I can report that specific features (e.g., update age, position anomalies, CTR decay) are strongly associated with a declining organic traffic trend.\n",
        "- **Directional Priority:** I can rank pages such that pages at the top of the queue have a significantly higher measured rate of traffic decline than those at the bottom.\n",
        "- **Decision Support:** I can provide an evidence-backed ranking that helps content editors allocate review capacity more efficiently than standard chronological or random sorting.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What my work will NEVER be able to claim:**\n",
        "- **Causal Proof:** I cannot claim that updating a page will *cause* a traffic recovery, as we have no controlled A/B experiment data to isolate the effect of a refresh.\n",
        "- **Predicting Google's Algorithm:** I cannot claim that the model explains or predicts Google's proprietary search ranking factors; we only measure historical search console outcomes."
